			<item>
				<title>FireFlow - HTB Machine Writeup</title>
				<link>http://localhost:1313/myblog/posts/fireflow/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 06 Jul 2026 10:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>http://localhost:1313/myblog/posts/fireflow/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;fireflow---hack-the-box-machine-writeup&#34;&gt;FireFlow - Hack The Box Machine Writeup&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Machine:&lt;/strong&gt; FireFlow&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;strong&gt;Category:&lt;/strong&gt; Web, Kubernetes, RCE&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;strong&gt;Difficulty:&lt;/strong&gt; Hard&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;strong&gt;Author:&lt;/strong&gt; 4mN3s14&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;recon&#34;&gt;Recon&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Nmap scan revealed ports 22 (SSH) and 443 (HTTPS) open with a self-signed cert for &lt;code&gt;fireflow.htb&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;*.fireflow.htb&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-bash&#34; data-lang=&#34;bash&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;sudo nmap -sC -sV -vv -oA fireflow 10.129.244.214&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;PORT      STATE    SERVICE   VERSION&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;22/tcp    open     ssh       OpenSSH 9.6p1 Ubuntu&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;443/tcp   open     ssl/http  nginx&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Added &lt;code&gt;fireflow.htb&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;flow.fireflow.htb&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;code&gt;/etc/hosts&lt;/code&gt; after visiting the main page.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>About</title>
				<link>http://localhost:1313/myblog/about/</link>
				<pubDate>Thu, 11 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>http://localhost:1313/myblog/about/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;about-me&#34;&gt;About Me&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I&amp;rsquo;m &lt;strong&gt;Jonan&lt;/strong&gt;, better known online as &lt;strong&gt;4mN3s14&lt;/strong&gt;. I&amp;rsquo;m a computer security and forensics student, a CTF player with &lt;strong&gt;Dead Pirate Society&lt;/strong&gt;, and a technical writer who learns by taking systems apart and documenting what happens.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;My main interests are offensive security, reverse engineering, digital forensics, OSINT, malware analysis, and Linux internals. In CTFs and security labs, I work across:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Binary exploitation and return-oriented programming&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Web vulnerabilities and authentication flaws&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Cryptography and implementation mistakes&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Python jails, polyglots, and unusual language behavior&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Malware, rootkits, and Linux kernel security&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Enumeration, privilege escalation, and complete attack chains&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I prefer practical work over surface-level summaries. A useful write-up should explain the reasoning, failed assumptions, commands, code, evidence, and remediation well enough for someone else to reproduce the result. Flags and sensitive values are redacted when they do not add educational value.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
